{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/155749965092735/posts/761737901160602/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/155749965092735/posts/761737901160602/","title":"Indian Shrimp Culture | Calculation for quantity of Bleaching Powder :- | Facebook","description":"Calculation for quantity of Bleaching Powder :-\n\n• Recommended dosage 10 to 15 ppm active chlorine (10 ppm for example)\n• 1 ppm = 1 mg/litre of water or 1 gram per tonne of water (10 ppm means 10 g...","language":"en","text":"What is the recommended dosage of bleaching powder for 15,000 m3?\n\nTitles are generated by AI from Meta\n\nCalculation for quantity of Bleaching Powder :-\n\n• Recommended dosage 10 to 15 ppm active chlorine (10 ppm for example)\n\n• 1 ppm = 1 mg/litre of water or 1 gram per tonne of water (10 ppm means 10 g per tonne or m3)\n\n• Example 1 ha pond with 1.5 m water (1 ha= 10,000m2)\n\n• Total volume of water = 10,000 x 1.5 = 15,000 m3\n\n• Quantity of chlorine required = 10 x 15,000 = 150000 g or 150 Kg\n\n• Bleaching powder contains 30-33% chlorine (say 30%), so 1 Kg of bleaching powder contains only 300 g chlorine (0.3 kg)\n\n• So for achieving 150 Kg chlorine , divide 150/0.3 = 500 Kg bleaching powder.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":1397.5692989770323,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}